  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If your roof insurance claim is denied, read the denial letter carefully, get a second opinion with photo proof from a local independent roofer, request a formal re-inspection, and file an appeal. If the insurer still refuses to pay, you can hire a public adjuster or file a state insurance board complaint.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Steps to Take"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Read the Denial Letter: Find the exact reason for the rejection (such as normal wear and tear, pre-existing damage, or lack of maintenance).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review Your Policy: Check your declarations page to confirm what types of storm, wind, or hail damage your policy covers.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Inspection: Hire a trusted local roofing contractor to inspect the roof, take clear photos, and write an independent damage report.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Request a Re-Inspection: Call your insurance company to ask for a re-inspection, and have your private roofer present when the insurance adjuster returns.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "How to Fight the Denial"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "File a Formal Appeal: Submit your contractor\u2019s written report, date-stamped photos, local weather reports, and repair estimates to your insurer via certified mail.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hire a Public Adjuster: Bring in an independent public adjuster who works for you (not the insurance company) to re-evaluate the damage and negotiate a settlement.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File a State Complaint: If you believe the insurer acted unfairly, file a complaint with your state\u2019s department of insurance.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Consult an Attorney: If the claim is high-value and you suspect bad faith denial, speak with an attorney who specializes in property insurance disputes.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              6
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow down your next step, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What reason did the insurance company give in the denial letter?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Was the damage caused by hail, wind, or age?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
